{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception interface, separating motion commands from sensor outcomes. The specification automaton enforces safe, coverage-oriented exploration: random_walk is preferred in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and recovery turns are used only when obstacles are detected. Recovery is conservative and always returns to exploration as soon as the path is clear. Full_rotate is used only as a last-resort scan after repeated blockages.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion and perception to keep the model modular.",
    "Specification automaton encodes the exploration policy: random_walk in clear, move_forward for short progress, rotate_clockwise/counterclockwise for obstacle recovery, and full_rotate only after repeated blockages."
  ],
